Rationale: The claim has two material parts: (1) Eucosma hennei has been found in California with a larval host organism, and (2) this organism and the genus Nymphoides (resembling water lily) are both types of plants. The second part is supported by multiple pieces of evidence confirming that Nymphoides is a plant genus. However, the first part remains insufficiently evidenced, as all searches for the larval host organism of Eucosma hennei in California returned no usable information. No evidence contradicts the claim, but further investigation is needed to confirm the first part.
